The Amidah blessing for redemption is called Geulah (“Redemption”), often beginning with Re’eh Na Ve’onyenu (“See our affliction”). Here is a clear English version:

Amidah – Prayer for Redemption (Geulah)

See our affliction and take up our cause,
and redeem us speedily for the sake of Your Name.

For You are a mighty redeemer.
Blessed are You, Lord,
the Redeemer of Israel.

=============================================================
Slightly expanded traditional-style translation:

Look upon our suffering and plead our cause,
and redeem us soon for the sake of Your Name;
for You are a powerful redeemer.

Blessed are You, Lord,
Redeemer of Israel.
